{
  "why": "Two worked documents, held as JSON rather than as TypeScript literals so that changing a figure is a diff in a data file and not a diff in the code that reads it. Every date is in 2027 or 2028, so no value here can coincide with the real clock: a fixture whose date happens to match today tests nothing about where the date came from. The regime is NOT in this file — the tests ask the registry for it, so the number format, the jurisdiction names and the component order are the real ones and not a copy that agrees by inspection.",

  "company": {
    "why": "The supplier. Registered in Tamil Nadu (state code 33), trading under a name that differs from its registered one — so the template has to print both, and a mapper that printed only one would be visible. It carries no logo, no bank details, no terms and no signatory, because migration 0011 has nowhere to put them; that absence is the point of the seam and there is a test that the page degrades cleanly without them.",
